WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:09.179
In 1948, Harvard historian Arthur
Schlesinger surveyed academic experts

00:00:09.179 --> 00:00:12.719
to conduct the first poll on
presidential greatness. The group named

00:00:12.719 --> 00:00:16.379
six great presidents: Lincoln, Washington,
FDR,

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:21.090
Wilson, Jefferson, and Jackson. Only
Lincoln got all 55 votes for the top

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:25.439
rank. According to Schlesinger, the
great's had a lot in common. All were

00:00:25.439 --> 00:00:29.340
identified with a crucial turning point;
all took timely actions to achieve

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:35.040
timeless results; all took the side of
reform. They were all party men; all were

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.390
strong, and has strong leaders they
aroused strong opposition; and none was a

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:43.290
great administrator. Since that time,
there had been many more surveys of

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:50.879
historians. C-SPAN conducted such surveys
in 2000, 2009, and 2017, and in all three

00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:55.980
Lincoln was first overall, followed by
George Washington and FDR. In a December

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:00.870
2016 Fox News survey of registered
voters, 11% said Trump would be one of

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:07.740
the greatest presidents and 25% above
average. 31% expected him to be one of the worst.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:11.250
Which of the six great
presidents do you think was the greatest?

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:15.780
Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know
what other topics you'd like our

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:20.159
scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be
sure to like and subscribe for more

00:01:20.159 --> 00:01:23.720
research and videos from AEI.

